=== CLARIFICATION of the three non-zero greps above ===
Every one is a COMMENT DISCLAIMING the thing, not code implementing it. Verified by inspection:

  MixtureThermodynamics.hpp:51  "NO CHEMISTRY. No reaction, no stoichiometry, no Arrhenius, no heat
                                 release, and no formation enthalpy"
                                 -> accounts for BOTH the Arrhenius and the stoichiom hit.
  MixtureThermodynamics.cpp:107 "disagree. Nothing is renormalised."
                                 -> the comment explaining WHY P18.1's validation is not duplicated.

So: NO chemistry, NO stoichiometry, NO Arrhenius, NO heat release, NO formation enthalpy, and NO
normalisation call anywhere in the new code.

The greps are recorded AS RUN rather than tightened to exclude comments, because a grep that skips
comments could also skip a real occurrence. Reporting the raw count and resolving it by inspection
is the safer direction.

